{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2883 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3bae5b1e5e4baf066248b0ab0c71664de7653e1f8341dd57090f311ed35db9b6" :edb/db-before-t 2882 :edb/db-after-t 2883 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536195 50 #inst "2026-10-09T19:31:22.319Z" 13194139536195 true] [17592186119756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388312 13194139536195 true] [17592186119756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388369 13194139536195 true] [17592186119756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388376 13194139536195 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388290 13194139536195 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388319 13194139536195 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388326 13194139536195 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388333 13194139536195 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388297 13194139536195 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388340 13194139536195 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388348 13194139536195 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388355 13194139536195 true] [17592186119759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388304 13194139536195 true] [17592186119759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388362 13194139536195 true] [17592186119759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388383 13194139536195 true] [17592186120170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536195 true] [17592186120170 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(8, 3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$\\frac{x + 2}{4} = \\frac{y - 1}{3} = \\frac{z - 2}{-1}$." 13194139536195 false] [17592186120170 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(8,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x+2}{4}=\\frac{y-1}{3}=\\frac{z-2}{-1}.$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186120170 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨8,3,-1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,3,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨4,3,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =⟨8,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z-42 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388291 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1089 "q-128376" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-5,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=3+t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=7-t\\end{aligned}.$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1113 #uuid "73a51566-e903-5429-a833-3a965966f7dc" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388290 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨1,1,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨1,1,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388292 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388293 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388294 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388295 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388296 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1041 "selection" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388295 13194139536195 true] [17592186388291 1110 #uuid "e3cf2ec3-b08f-5c28-b812-c14f968dc777" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388292 1034 "x-y+z-6=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388292 1111 #uuid "e2594059-827b-55b5-8208-d8a00afb06f6" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388293 1034 "-x-y+z+1=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388293 1111 #uuid "773ac187-9f1a-5da9-b359-cb81e454cded" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388294 1034 "x-y-z+3=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388294 1111 #uuid "45896f8a-7944-531c-893e-522a8af1d878" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388295 1034 "x+y-z+6=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388295 1111 #uuid "0f03d236-ebd3-5571-9e7b-706d5d055a76" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388296 1034 "x+y+z-3=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388296 1111 #uuid "f8f4ca43-67ad-54b5-88d2-654580ef9be5" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388298 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1089 "q-128400" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1100 "Given the Cartesian equation $7x+y-3=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1113 #uuid "a275fd86-a21a-5ef1-ae5c-9df806e069b0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388297 1145 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨7,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+y-3 & =0 \\\\ y & =3-7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,3,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,3,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388299 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388300 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388301 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388302 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388303 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1041 "selection" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388302 13194139536195 true] [17592186388298 1110 #uuid "10b864a4-1db5-53bd-a23e-5baed302ea88" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388299 1034 "(r-⟨0,-3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,0⟩=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388299 1111 #uuid "9b591e97-568e-54e1-b2ff-3b25d6f8a868" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388300 1034 "(r-⟨0,9,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨-7,0,1⟩=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388300 1111 #uuid "8bfbc34b-25a5-5d23-bc9c-f80e7085e552" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388301 1034 "(r-⟨0,6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,1⟩=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388301 1111 #uuid "1f0a58eb-4f3d-598b-8f9e-aaeb7207b6f1" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388302 1034 "(r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388302 1111 #uuid "990652fd-70a4-5d37-8d07-9f27ede2f633" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388303 1034 "(r-⟨0,-6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,0,1⟩=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388303 1111 #uuid "75ce8e92-2131-5643-828a-adff4a01a923" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388305 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388308 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388310 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1089 "q-326312" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,-2,-5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,1,-7⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y+z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1113 #uuid "11d73e76-733c-5c1a-b58a-cd0a522da6dc" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388304 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-3,2,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =19i+7j+k \\\\  & =⟨19,7,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =⟨-3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =-39\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =-39 \\\\ 19x+7y+z & =-39 \\\\ 19x+7y+z+39 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388306 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388307 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1041 "field-1" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388306 13194139536195 true] [17592186388305 1110 #uuid "904b214a-ae22-5da8-80b3-34896b7bc41c" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388306 1034 "19" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388306 1111 #uuid "ed723e51-f1a8-57b1-8bcc-cbd523f467cf" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388307 1034 "18" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388307 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388307 1111 #uuid "778b5a41-2ec5-55c3-b9ae-e8c86cf0ff20" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388309 13194139536195 true] [17592186388308 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536195 true] [17592186388308 1041 "field-2" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388308 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388309 13194139536195 true] [17592186388308 1110 #uuid "9c61baff-428f-5056-b452-d1bac27bc5ce" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388309 1034 "7" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388309 1111 #uuid "1393e66b-02fc-5824-8c21-c9d22567df56" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388310 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388311 13194139536195 true] [17592186388310 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536195 true] [17592186388310 1041 "field-3" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388310 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388311 13194139536195 true] [17592186388310 1110 #uuid "35957583-1ed3-5158-8d03-b280590e6b8c" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388311 1034 "39" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388311 1111 #uuid "6e575f31-f881-5e2d-8d93-b41a75073669" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388313 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1089 "q-33067" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(5,0,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,4,-1⟩.$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1113 #uuid "19fdb04a-9367-5fe1-9cea-0be46faa4ebc" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388312 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨5,0,-3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨2,4,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =⟨5,0,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z-13 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388314 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388315 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388316 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388317 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388318 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1041 "selection" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388318 13194139536195 true] [17592186388313 1110 #uuid "c094f0b7-fb1e-5ddb-8ade-9f0e68866fda" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388314 1034 "x+y-z-18=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388314 1111 #uuid "3772d1eb-4c9f-5d5b-b49f-8f0e29c2b36f" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388315 1034 "2x+4y+z+5=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388315 1111 #uuid "124474af-26ba-5dda-98d6-37a32065d8e1" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388316 1034 "5x+y-3z-13=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388316 1111 #uuid "08c56b76-bc81-5a59-8402-593bf00cce7b" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388317 1034 "5x-3z-13=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388317 1111 #uuid "849db852-c8cb-556f-9638-60d492ba681a" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388318 1034 "2x+4y-z-13=0" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536195 true] [17592186388318 1111 #uuid "9293726e-4e2e-5cd8-bfdc-60c58b378cf6" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388320 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1089 "q-33162" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,0,4)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1113 #uuid "c43b9462-37b6-5478-904d-7307590edba1" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388319 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-5,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-5,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-1 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z & =-1 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388321 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388322 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388323 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388324 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388325 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1041 "selection" 13194139536195 true] [17592186388320 1104 #edb/ref 17592186